cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sloptrim: a deterministic prose-quality detector and always-on writing contract"
message: "If you use this software or the measurements cited below, please cite it. This is a pre-1.0 release; the interfaces and the score calibration may still change."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hadi
    given-names: Seyed Ehsan
repository-code: "https://github.com/seyedehsanhadi/sloptrim"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.9.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
keywords:
  - writing quality
  - text analysis
  - stylometry
  - large language models
  - research software
abstract: >-
  sloptrim scores prose against a catalogue of 71 documented patterns of
  machine-flavoured writing and asks the writer to fix what it flags. 62 of the
  71 have a detector in scripts/detect.py; the other 9 need a reading. Thirteen
  of the 62 rules are held out of the score as markers of formal register or of
  typesetting rather than of machine authorship. They fall on thirteen
  catalogue numbers, but number 17 keeps a second rule that still scores, so 12
  numbers carry no weight and 50 still do. The detector is deterministic, uses
  only the Python standard library, and opens no socket, which a test enforces
  by walking every script in the repository. It is a writing-quality
  instrument and not an authorship classifier: the score counts documented
  patterns and says nothing about who or what wrote the document.

  A public matched benchmark contains five experiments with 30 human and 30
  machine articles per arm. Sloptrim's score achieved ROC-AUC 0.762 to 0.946
  across GPT-4o, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, o1-pro, paraphrased GPT-4o and humanized
  o1-pro. A separate date-stamped 30-pair GPT-5.6 Sol run achieved ROC-AUC
  0.965, while the normal guard threshold flagged none of its generated
  articles and strict mode flagged 12 of 30. These are style-ranking results,
  not evidence of authorship. The protocol, confidence intervals, source
  revision, hashes and limitations are recorded in
  docs/research/frontier-benchmark-results.md.
